{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ROOT-CAUSE EVIDENCE, captured BEFORE any kickstart (this ticket's first AC requires that ordering —\nforcing a sync first would have destroyed it).\n\n`launchctl print gui/$(id -u)/com.navapbc.rebar-dev-update`:\n    state          = not running\n    run interval   = 3600 seconds\n    properties     = runatload | inferred program\n    LAST EXIT CODE = 1\n    stdout path    = /Users/joeoakhart/.local/state/rebar-dev/launchd.out.log\n    stderr path    = /Users/joeoakhart/.local/state/rebar-dev/launchd.err.log\n\nSO THE AGENT IS NOT IDLE — IT IS FIRING HOURLY AND FAILING EVERY TIME. That distinction matters: a\nstopped agent looks like a stopped agent, whereas this one is alive, scheduled, and silently\nunsuccessful, which is why nobody noticed for days.\n\nTHREE CORROBORATING TIMESTAMPS in /Users/joeoakhart/.local/state/rebar-dev/:\n    launchd.err.log   0 bytes, created Jul 10 12:03\n    launchd.out.log   0 bytes, created Jul 10 12:03\n    last-good.sha     41 bytes, Jul 17 08:16\n    directory mtime   Jul 31 21:47  (i.e. TODAY, minutes before this capture)\n\nRead together: the directory is touched on every run, so the agent DID run today; it exits 1; and it\nhas written NOTHING to either log since the files were created on Jul 10. **An updater that fails\nhourly with exit 1 and produces zero diagnostic output is the real defect** — the stale build is only\nits symptom. Whatever fails, fails before any redirection takes effect, or its output is discarded.\n\nThe last recorded GOOD sha is Jul 17, while the installed\nsite-packages/rebar/llm/criteria/overlay.py is dated Jul 27 17:10. So the rollback guard is pinning a\nJul-27 build while the last verified-good checkpoint is ten days older still — the two records\ndisagree, and neither matches origin/main.\n\nDO NOT kickstart before capturing whatever the underlying script writes when run by hand: the\n0-byte logs mean the launchd redirection is not carrying its output, so run the updater's script\ndirectly in a shell to see the actual error. Kickstarting first re-runs it under the same broken\nredirection and yields the same silence."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785562777519462001,"uuid":"979ed831-837d-429d-bd92-b780d950b73c"}